course: dictionary
lesson: 6032
title: Melodious: words that sound sweet
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Melodious describes something with a pleasant tune that is sweet and pleasing to hear. You can use it for a song, birdsong or a voice. Poets often call nightingales and blackbirds melodious. When you meet the word, listen for the clues: is the sound nice, or harsh and jangly?
explain: Read this: «Her melodious voice filled the hall.» The word voice tells you we are talking about sound, and filled the hall tells you it was loud enough to fill a space. The word melodious tells you the sound was sweet, not shouting. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Her sweet, pleasing voice filled the hall" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Notice that melodious is about how something sounds to our ears. Many people find Ukrainian melodious, which is an opinion about how the language sounds. Be careful with claims: «the story that it won a world contest as the second most melodious language after Italian has no real source.» A word can describe a sound, but a story about a sound still needs proof.
fact: Melodious means having a pleasant tune, sweet and pleasing to hear.
fact: Melodious is an adjective. The adverb is melodiously, as in «she hummed melodiously».
fact: Melodious can describe songs, birdsong and voices: «a melodious voice», «melodious song».
fact: Melodious describes how something sounds, so it is an opinion: people may find different sounds melodious.
fact: Some claims sound true but have no real source. Check before you repeat them.
exercise: «The melodious song drifted through the open window.» What does melodious mean? | Very slow and dull | Dark and cold | Loud and angry | *Having a pleasant, sweet tune
exercise: «Her melodious voice filled the hall.» Which word tells you the voice sounds sweet? | hall | *melodious | her | filled
exercise: Many people find Ukrainian melodious. What does this suggest? | Many people cannot speak it at all | It has no words in it | *Many people think it sounds sweet and pleasing | It is the loudest language in the world
test: «The melodious birdsong woke the village.» What does melodious mean here? | *Sweet and pleasing to hear | Loud and harsh | Dusty | Silent
test: «The singer hummed melodiously.» How was she humming? | Roughly and badly | *In a sweet, pleasing tune | Very fast | Without making any sound
exam: «The story that Ukrainian was crowned the most melodious language has no real source.» Is this story proven? | *No, it has no real source | Yes, every book says so | Yes, it won a world contest | Yes, a famous poet wrote it down
